{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YJK"}],"opens":"A branch is a store, and unlike git's, relational: no longer stale, still a branch, seen from the front as a whole rather than from the side as a fork; this series itself a store of its own. A valuable future development of the store.","restsOn":["taking a whole away as a store","how stores relate to the stores they branched from"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XET","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A branch as a store"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YJK"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YP8"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YQ8"}],"opens":"Not login but proof: a commit's hash set into a public chain proves a series of events was observed in a particular way from a certain point in time, and no one can mask over it after; only the hash goes public, the store stays its owner's.","restsOn":["signing commits by key","which public chain, and what anchoring costs"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XEV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"History anchored in public"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YJK"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YQ8"}],"opens":"No backend for auth: public data encrypted to the degree the data itself is built upon, so whoever holds the key reads, and authority is in the keys and not in a server. Asked from curiosity about the nature of authority, not as a direction.","restsOn":["how keys are held and given","what is encrypted, and at which holon"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XEW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Authority held in keys"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YQ8"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YTJ"}],"opens":"A piece closed, then observable, then closed and observable again; invisible holons on other holons; and prose at the fidelity one is attuned to, a sentence a string or its words, recursable, a string the closed form and its holons the open one.","restsOn":["whether a string is ever stored or only drawn","what is not yet in a holon: to enter, reachable, or created"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XEX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Pieces opened and closed"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YTJ"}],"opens":"A word's meaning is only its relations within the field; on that, primitive patterns: knowledge graphs upon terms, and other components; terms perhaps not functional without something of more breadth, like symbols. Landscape, levels, holarchies and systems as one family of words.","restsOn":["what a symbol is beside a term","the types of prose, drafted, not confirmed"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XEY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Ontology in the field"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001YZH"}],"opens":"A larger piece read in whole, then drawn over by isolated readers, each a branch of its own: the top of the gradient over a large quantity of holons, what matters changing with height, a steering made and then forgotten so the branches stand further apart; new ways of digesting branches made from them.","restsOn":["a branch as a store","what a digest of branches is"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XEZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Many branches over one held space"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001Z5D"}],"opens":"Every run and saved store read under one union, since holons are holons and the union is always divisible again by them; sessions coordinating around one available state, unintrusive by nature, each adding and none rewriting another's.","restsOn":["a union as a reading of stores, not a store that moves them","the licence boundary as a store boundary"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A union of stores"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001Z5D"}],"opens":"Branches drawn across variables, model from the most basic to the highest, seed from inside or outside the held space, with unifying points held fixed across them: the same base, the same brief, the same seed across models.","restsOn":["which models can be reached","a digest that reads a matrix, not a list"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A matrix of readers"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZBN"}],"opens":"Everything derived over the store is a function of it: statistics declared as functional data, in prose and in expression, drawn by the interface whenever looked at and never kept as results; and a completion model that streams slots, expressions and interfaces natively, not markdown.","restsOn":["functions that count and measure","streams, being specced by the first session","native prose"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Statistics declared, not stored"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZEM"}],"opens":"Each session is its own; sessions only converge, where their timelines or their holons touch, across a certain degree of order and linearity. What one says stays its own, and another meets it by reference, never by holding a copy.","restsOn":["a convergence as a reference between sessions, said from either side"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Sessions converge, never copy"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZM6"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZQM"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0002072"}],"opens":"The store stays in git, as the site publishes its field as it stands, but not as one loose file per object, which grows with every holon, nor as one file, which every publish rewrites: as packs that never change, one per commit, each holding only what that commit adds, with an index read by range from any static host; growth linear in what changes, and the first birth itself cut into commits at a realistic fidelity, since the whole is structural and its evolution topologically divisible. Files divide two ways: by ownership and wholeness, a store per whole, branch as store; and by time, a pack per commit. What may need forgetting is kept as a store of its own, apart from git until sure; a store can always be picked up, left, worked on and come back to. The birth from markdown may end here: the holons are the source now, and any birth after only produces diff-packs. Git is the carrier of the store's files, never its model.","restsOn":["the file backend writing packs and their indexes","store.md and remotes.md rewritten for packs","glass not based on git, the author's of 2026-11-01"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"The store packed, carried by git"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZW2"},{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001ZZN"}],"opens":"A store's point is sometimes not to forget but to pack up and leave: a whole that rests upon another, pointing into it, and stands when carried away, as a stream buffer does. And forgetting is allowed: lifetimes exist, and the end of a thing is decided at the point of its creation. Inference runs are large; the analysis upon them goes as deep as it goes and is made separate, and the runs beneath it may end when their lifetime does. Storage is hot and cold as well, parts of reality; a store given a real lifetime, as things are locked or expired in a bucket. A capacity for the future, pointed to, not yet built.","restsOn":["a store declaring its lifetime, by contract","storage that honours it: retention and expiry","streams, being specced by the first session"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Stores that rest on stores, with a lifetime"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G000209A"}],"opens":"The markdown dropped but for what lets a new session digest the store in a noble manner: an entry into it and a way to read any holon back as text; and soon a new glass for human interface, an evolved experience based upon this store.","restsOn":["the store code brought to the primitives as they stand","packs","an interface that reads the union"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"A glass for the human, born from the store"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00020YA"}],"opens":"Within a store everything is finite, so holons are simply counted, 1, 2, 3, by order and locality of birth, a reference within the store only its number. Nothing needs to be unique until stores meet: a union gives each store a prefix, as a mount gives a directory its place, and a store born of another is named by its parent, which counts its children. Names are then relative to the union that reads them; randomness, a key or a hash is needed only for a name meant to mean the same in every union, and can wait until it is. The prefix says where a holon was born, never where it stands, which stays a route.","restsOn":["one writer per store, branch as store","how a union assigns its prefixes","the code brought to the store"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Names counted in locality, unified where stores meet"}
{"body":{"from":[{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00020YA"}],"opens":"The store is append-only, so where bytes are written never changes, and an object's address is its place: segment, offset, length. A hash on every object names everything twice, beside the holon's own identity, and costs near half the store with the indexes it forces; it is let go. Segments are one per publish, not per commit, so files are as few as publishes. Each commit keeps one sha256, a fixed-length fingerprint of the bytes it added and of its parent's: a hash of hashes, so one stands for the whole history, any part provable by a path that grows by one step each time what lies beneath doubles. And the lexicon a whole that grows by its parts, not one body rewritten at every new word.","restsOn":["the pack format rewritten to segments and offsets","the code brought to the store"],"stands":"noted"},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001XF8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000007"],"name":"Addresses by position, one fingerprint per commit"}
